#!/bin/sh
# mkrepopage DIR: index.html for the repo in DIR (DIR/x86_64, DIR/x86 and the key), with a list-ARCH.tsv of every
# package mag can install from the repos in REPOS, for the search on it
set -e
[ $# = 1 ] && [ -d "$1/x86_64" ] || { echo "usage: mkrepopage DIR" >&2; exit 2; }
dir=$1
here=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)
repos=${REPOS:-$here/pkg/chamesle-base/repos}
tmp=$(mktemp -d "$dir/.page.XXXXXX")
trap 'rm -rf "$tmp"' EXIT

esc() { sed 's/&/\&amp;/g; s/</\&lt;/g; s/>/\&gt;/g'; }

# idx FILE REPO: name, version, repo, installed size, description and dependencies, a line each
idx() {
	tar -xzOf "$1" APKINDEX | awk -v r="$2" -F: '
		/^P:/ { p = substr($0, 3) } /^V:/ { v = substr($0, 3) } /^I:/ { i = substr($0, 3) }
		/^T:/ { t = substr($0, 3); gsub(/\t/, " ", t) }
		/^D:/ { n = split(substr($0, 3), x, " "); d = ""; for (j = 1; j <= n; j++) if (x[j] !~ /^(so|pc|cmd):/) d = d (d == "" ? "" : " ") x[j] }
		/^$/ { if (p != "") print p "\t" v "\t" r "\t" i "\t" t "\t" d; p = v = i = t = d = "" }
		END { if (p != "") print p "\t" v "\t" r "\t" i "\t" t "\t" d }'
}

for a in x86_64 x86; do
	: > "$tmp/$a"
	while read -r u; do
		case $u in ''|'#'*) continue;; esac
		case $u in
		*chamesle.org/repo*) f=$dir/$a/APKINDEX.tar.gz r=chamesle;;
		*) f=$tmp/$a.idx r=${u##*/}; curl -fsSL "$u/$a/APKINDEX.tar.gz" -o "$f";;
		esac
		idx "$f" "$r" >> "$tmp/$a"
	done < "$repos"
	sort -t "$(printf '\t')" -k1,1 -u "$tmp/$a" > "$dir/list-$a.tsv"
done

own() {
	tar -xzOf "$dir/$1/APKINDEX.tar.gz" APKINDEX | awk -F: '
		/^P:/ { p = substr($0, 3) } /^V:/ { v = substr($0, 3) } /^S:/ { s = substr($0, 3) }
		/^I:/ { i = substr($0, 3) } /^T:/ { t = substr($0, 3) } /^D:/ { d = substr($0, 3) }
		/^$/ { if (p != "") print p "|" v "|" s "|" i "|" t "|" d; p = v = s = i = t = d = "" }
		END { if (p != "") print p "|" v "|" s "|" i "|" t "|" d }' |
	while IFS='|' read -r p v s i t d; do
		f=$p-$v.apk
		sum=$(sha256sum "$dir/$1/$f" | cut -c1-64)
		deps=
		for x in $d; do deps="$deps <a href=\"#$x\">$x</a>"; done
		printf '<tr><td><b>%s</b><br>%s</td><td>%s</td><td>%s K<br>%s K installed</td><td><a href="%s/%s">%s</a><br><code class="sum">%s</code></td></tr>\n' \
			"$p" "$v" "$(printf '%s' "$t" | esc)${deps:+<br><small>needs$deps</small>}" "$1" "$((s / 1024))" "$((i / 1024))" "$1" "$f" "$f" "$sum"
	done
}

key=$(ls "$dir"/*.rsa.pub | head -1)
fp=$(openssl pkey -pubin -in "$key" -outform DER | sha256sum | cut -c1-64)
now=$(date +%Y-%m-%d)
n64=$(wc -l < "$dir/list-x86_64.tsv")

cat > "$dir/index.html" <<H
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Repo - Chamesle</title>
<meta name="description" content="Chamesle's package repo, and a search over every package mag can install.">
<link rel="canonical" href="https://chamesle.org/repo/">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../style.css?19">
<link rel="icon" href="../img/logo.png">
<style>
#q { width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font: inherit; padding: 4px; }
#hits td, .own td { vertical-align: top; }
.sum { font-size: 11px; word-break: break-all; }
.pkg { margin: 12px 0; padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #888; }
.pkg pre { margin: 6px 0 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div id="page">

<div id="top">
<h1><a href="../"><img src="../img/banner-dark.png" alt="Chamesle Linux" width="223" height="56"></a></h1>
</div>

<div id="nav">
<a href="../">Home</a> |
<a href="../download.html">Download</a> |
<a href="../docs.html">Handbook</a> |
<a href="../packages.html">Packages</a> |
<b>Repo</b> |
<a href="../new.html">News</a> |
<a href="../board.html">Board</a> |
<a href="../source.html">Source</a> |
<a href="../about.html">About</a>
</div>

<main>
<h2>The repo</h2>
<p><code>https://chamesle.org/repo</code> has Chamesle's own packages, for <code>x86_64</code> and <code>x86</code>.
mag reads it next to the musl repo with everything else; both are in <code>/etc/mag/repos</code> of every install.
The index and every package are signed with <a href="$(basename "$key")">$(basename "$key")</a>, whose key has the
SHA-256 <code class="sum">$fp</code></p>
<pre>https://chamesle.org/repo
cp $(basename "$key") /etc/mag/keys/</pre>

<h2>Search</h2>
<p>Every package mag can install, $n64 of them for x86_64. <label><input type="radio" name="arch" value="x86_64" checked> x86_64</label>
<label><input type="radio" name="arch" value="x86"> x86</label></p>
<input id="q" type="search" placeholder="a name or a word, like tmux or irc" autocomplete="off">
<div id="pkg"></div>
<table id="hits"></table>

<h2>Chamesle's packages</h2>
<h3>x86_64</h3>
<table class="own">
$(own x86_64)
</table>
<h3>x86</h3>
<table class="own">
$(own x86)
</table>
</main>

<hr>
<div id="foot">
Made by <code>mkrepopage</code> from <a href="https://github.com/tortr-rs/system">system</a> on $now.
</div>

</div>

<script>
var lists = {}, arch = 'x86_64', q = document.getElementById('q'), hits = document.getElementById('hits'), one = document.getElementById('pkg');
function e(s) { return s.replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;'); }
function load(a, then) {
	if (lists[a]) return then();
	fetch('list-' + a + '.tsv').then(function (r) { return r.text(); }).then(function (t) {
		var m = {}, l = t.split('\\n').filter(Boolean).map(function (x) { var f = x.split('\\t'); m[f[0]] = f; return f; });
		lists[a] = { all: l, by: m }; then();
	});
}
function find() {
	var w = q.value.trim().toLowerCase(), l = lists[arch].all, out = [];
	if (w.length < 2) { hits.innerHTML = ''; return; }
	l.forEach(function (f) {
		var n = f[0].toLowerCase(), r = n == w ? 0 : n.indexOf(w) == 0 ? 1 : n.indexOf(w) > 0 ? 2 : f[4].toLowerCase().indexOf(w) >= 0 ? 3 : -1;
		if (r >= 0) out.push([r, f]);
	});
	out.sort(function (a, b) { return a[0] - b[0] || a[1][0].localeCompare(b[1][0]); });
	hits.innerHTML = out.slice(0, 100).map(function (x) {
		var f = x[1];
		return '<tr><td><a href="#' + e(f[0]) + '">' + e(f[0]) + '</a></td><td>' + e(f[1]) + '</td><td>' + e(f[4]) + '</td></tr>';
	}).join('') + (out.length > 100 ? '<tr><td colspan="3"><i>' + (out.length - 100) + ' more, say more</i></td></tr>' : '');
}
function show() {
	var n = decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1)), f = lists[arch] && lists[arch].by[n];
	if (!n) { one.innerHTML = ''; return; }
	if (!f) { one.innerHTML = '<div class="pkg">no <b>' + e(n) + '</b> for ' + arch + '</div>'; return; }
	var d = f[5] ? f[5].split(' ').map(function (x) { var b = x.replace(/[<>=~].*/, '').replace(/^so:|^cmd:|^pc:/, ''); return lists[arch].by[b] ? '<a href="#' + e(b) + '">' + e(x) + '</a>' : e(x); }).join(' ') : 'nothing';
	one.innerHTML = '<div class="pkg"><b>' + e(f[0]) + '</b> ' + e(f[1]) + ', from ' + e(f[2]) + ', ' + Math.round(f[3] / 1024) + ' K installed<br>' + e(f[4]) + '<br><small>needs ' + d + '</small><pre>mag install ' + e(f[0]) + '</pre></div>';
}
document.querySelectorAll('input[name=arch]').forEach(function (r) { r.onchange = function () { arch = r.value; load(arch, function () { find(); show(); }); }; });
q.oninput = find;
window.onhashchange = show;
load(arch, function () { find(); show(); });
</script>
</body>
</html>
H
echo "$dir/index.html: $n64 packages for x86_64"
